"termsAndConditions_description" = "Dear user,\n\nWelcome to use the products and/or services provided by [ECBOT Limited] (hereinafter referred to as \"ECBOT\" or \"we\") through this tongue imaging APP and its extensions (hereinafter referred to as the SERVICE). Before you start using our service and experience our full range of products and We want to assure you that our first priority is our firm commitment to the security and privacy of your personal information. Fully recognizing the importance of information security, we are unswervingly committed to ensuring that your personal information receives the most appropriate security protection.\n\nThis privacy policy applies to all information you provide when accessing and using the SERVICE and all related products and services. This statement aims to explain in detail how we obtain, use, store, share and transfer your personal data, and will provide you with a series of rights and channels for information management such as inquiry, update, deletion, protection and account cancellation. \n\nBefore continuing to use the SERVICE, we kindly ask you to patiently and carefully read through and deeply understand all the terms and core points of this privacy policy. When you choose to accept and use our products and services, or continue to use them after we update the privacy policy from time to time (you will be notified of the update details in due course), you are deemed to fully agree and accept this privacy policy (including future versions) updated content), authorize us to collect, use, share and process your relevant information in accordance with this policy.\n\nThe following is the personal information protection policy we follow:\n\n(1)Definition of personal information: Personal information refers to various information elements recorded in electronic or other forms that can identify the identity of a specific natural person alone or in combination with other information, or reflect the activities of a specific natural person.\n\n(2)Compliance and legality: We strictly abide by the \"Cybersecurity Law of the People\'s Republic of China\", \"Personal Information Protection Law of the People\'s Republic of China\" and \"Information Security Technology Personal Information Security Specifications\" (GB/T 35273–2020) and Other relevant laws and regulations require that when you access the platform and use our services and/or products, your personal information will be collected and used only based on the principles of legitimacy, legality and necessity.\n\n(3)Notification and consent of expanded use: If in subsequent service operations, we need to use your personal information for other purposes not specified in this privacy policy, or apply the collected information to different scenarios for specific service needs. , we will make this clear to you in advance in a reasonable and transparent manner and obtain your explicit consent.\n\n(4)Anonymization processing and data analysis: After collecting your personal information, if it needs to be used for new purposes not covered by this privacy policy, we will use technical means to de-identify it to ensure that the information cannot be used alone or combined Other information to identify your true identity. Here, we would like to remind you that anonymized data does not constitute personal information that can identify you personally in the legal sense. Nonetheless, please know and agree that, without disclosing your personal information, we have the right to conduct group analysis and data mining on the user database, and provide marketing strategy suggestions and service optimization opinions based on test results accordingly.\n \n(5)Sharing of statistical information: We will collect statistics on the use of products and/or services, and may share such anonymized statistical information with the public or third parties in order to show overall usage trends. Please note that these shared statistics do not contain any details that can identify you, and any identifiable details have been anonymized as described in Section 4.\n\nWe deeply recognize the importance of personal information to you and go all out to maintain its security and reliability. We adhere to the basic principles of consistent rights and responsibilities, clear purpose, choice of consent, minimum use, ensuring security, subject participation and openness and transparency, and strive to protect the security of your personal information. At the same time, we promise to take strict protection measures based on the industry\'s mature security standards to ensure the security of your personal information.\n\nPlease read and fully understand this Privacy Policy before using our products (and services) to ensure that your rights and interests are fully respected and protected.\n\nThis Privacy Policy is designed to provide you with a clear and transparent guide to help you fully understand the following core contents:\n\n1.Collection and use of personal information\n\nWe explain in detail what personal information we collect from you and under what circumstances it is collected. At the same time, we will explain how to use this information legally, properly and necessaryly, including but not limited to providing services, improving product functions, personalized recommendations, user identity verification and ensuring account security.\n\n2.Sharing, transfer and public disclosure of personal information\n\nIn this section, we will clearly point out the circumstances under which your personal information may be shared with third parties, or necessary transfers due to legal regulations, business needs, etc., and the circumstances under which we will disclose it Disclose non-personally identifiable information or anonymized statistical information.\n\n3.Measures for storage, preservation and protection of personal information\n\nThis policy explains how we store and preserve your personal information, including the storage period, security protection measures, means and technical guarantees to prevent risks such as unauthorized access, public disclosure, use, modification, damage or loss.\n\n4.Application of Cookies and Other Tracking Technologies\n\nThis section explains how we use cookies and other similar technologies to improve user experience, analyze site traffic and user behavior patterns, and how to control the use of such technologies based on your preferences.\n\n5.Manage your personal information rights\n\nWe will guide you on how to query, correct, delete, restrict processing or withdraw your consent to the use of personal information, as well as how to apply to cancel your account, etc., to fully protect your right to manage your personal information.\n\n6.Special protection of minors’ personal information\n\nFor users under the legal age, we have clarified the specific principles and scope of obtaining and using their personal information, as well as the guardian consent mechanism, to ensure that we comply with the special protection requirements for minors\' personal information under applicable laws and regulations.\n\n7.Privacy Policy Updates and Notices\n\nWhen the privacy policy changes, we will explain the reasons for the update, the process and how to notify you of the update in a timely manner to ensure that you are always aware of and aware of our latest privacy protection measures.\n\n8.Contact information\n\nProvide an effective communication channel for you to consult, give feedback or lodge complaints with us regarding any privacy policy, personal information processing and other related issues.\n\n9.Dispute Resolution Mechanism\n\nIt describes the legal channels, mediation procedures and possible solutions we will follow when disputes involving personal information protection arise, to ensure that any disputes that may arise are properly handled.\n\n1.Collection and use of personal information\n\nIn order to provide you with a full range of services, we will collect and use your personal information legally and compliantly under the following scenarios and purposes:\n\n1.1.User account registration\n\nTo ensure that you can fully enjoy the various services of Traditional Chinese Medicine Tongue Diagnosis, you need to first authorize your mobile phone number on WeChat for real-name verification to register an account or use your email to register. If you choose not to provide your mobile phone number for verification, you may be unable to complete registration and use our products and services.\n\n1.2.Tongue health self-assessment service\n\nWhen providing the tongue health self-assessment function, we need to obtain your camera permission to take tongue photos. If you do not agree to grant this license, you will not be able to use the tongue detection service; but please note that this does not affect your use of other non-related services we provide. Based on the tongue pictures you upload, we will analyze tongue color, tooth marks, punctures, cracks, coating texture, coating color and other characteristics, and combine it with the database data to generate a comprehensive evaluation report, including individual evaluations of each indicator and Overall tongue interpretation. At the same time, we will provide you with personalized health suggestions based on the analysis results, such as dietary conditioning plans and traditional Chinese medicine health care guidance. Please note that factors such as the light and angle of the shooting environment may affect image quality and diagnostic accuracy.\n\n1.3.Personal information obtained indirectly\n\nWhen you choose to log in or use our products and services through a third-party platform such as WeChat, we may obtain and use some of your account information, such as avatar and nickname, from the third party based on your authorization. In addition, when you use the services provided by our affiliates and partners, you agree that we will receive, use, integrate and analyze information provided by third parties and their affiliates or partners based on actual business needs and with your explicit authorization. of personal information about you.\n\n1.4.Exceptions under specific circumstances\n\nAccording to relevant laws and regulations, we may collect and use your personal information without obtaining your prior informed consent under the following circumstances:\n(1)Matters involving national security and national defense security;\n(2)Relating to public safety, public health or major public interests;\n(3)Closely related to activities such as criminal investigation, prosecution, trial and judgment execution;\n(4)When it is necessary to protect your or other individuals’ life, property and other major legitimate rights and interests and it is difficult to obtain your consent;\n(5)Information that you have disclosed yourself;\n(6)We collect your personal information from legal public disclosure channels, such as news reports, government information disclosure, etc.;\n(7)Necessary according to the contract signing requirements;\n(8)To ensure the safe and stable operation of the products and services provided, such as troubleshooting and repair;\n(9)Necessary for legitimate news reporting;\n(10)Academic research institutions conduct statistical or academic research based on public interests, and have de-identified the personal information contained when publishing the research results;\n(11)Other special circumstances stipulated in laws and regulations.\n\n1.5.Legal basis consultation\n\nIf you have any questions about the legal basis for our collection and use of your personal information or need further information, please contact us by referring to the contact information in Chapter 8 \"How to Contact Us\".\n\n2.Rules for processing and disclosure of personal information\n\n2.1.Sharing of personal information\n\n2.1.1.We will not share your personal information with any company, organization or individual outside ECBOT without your explicit consent, unless the following special circumstances exist:\n\n(1)Explicit consent: We will share your personal information with other parties after obtaining your explicit consent.\n(2)Legal and regulatory requirements: Your personal information will be provided to external parties in accordance with legal and regulatory requirements or mandatory requirements of government authorities.\n(3)Core function service needs: In order to realize the core functions of our products and services or provide you with the services you need, when necessary, we will specifically prompt you and obtain your consent before sharing information.\n(4)Sharing with affiliated companies: With your consent, we will anonymize the information you provide and the information generated by using ECBOT services, and share it with ECBOT and its affiliated companies to provide better services, recommend products and develop markets Survey and data analysis. If affiliated companies need to change the purpose of information processing, they must seek your authorization again.\n\n2.1.2.At the same time, in order to provide a better service experience, we may share necessary personal information with authorized partners, but only for the purposes stated in this privacy policy. For example, in order to arrange logistics delivery during the purchase of products, we may need to share some personal information with logistics companies. All partners are strictly required to use shared information only within the legal, proper and necessary scope, and not for other purposes. We share information with the following types of partners:\n\n(1)Goods or technical service providers, such as communication, logistics, payment and other service providers, in order to complete core service links such as order processing, goods delivery and payment confirmation.\n(2)For promotion partners, we will conduct promotion effect analysis and feedback based on indirect user portrait data that cannot identify personal identity, but will not disclose your personally identifiable information.\n\n2.2.Transfer of personal information\n\nWe will not transfer your personal information at will, except in the following circumstances:\n(1)With your explicit consent, we will transfer your personal information to third parties.\n(2)In the event of a merger, division or bankruptcy liquidation, if a transfer of personal information is involved, we will inform the recipient of the information and ensure that the new holder continues to abide by this privacy policy, otherwise we will obtain your consent again.\n\n2.3.Public disclosure\n\nWe will publicly disclose your personal information only under the following circumstances:\n(1)With your explicit consent;\n(2)Required by laws and regulations or required by litigation procedures;\n(3)When we receive a legally binding request to disclose information, we will disclose it in compliance with laws and regulations.\n\n2.4.Situations where prior consent is not required\n\nUnder certain conditions, your personal information may be shared, transferred, or publicly disclosed without your prior authorization and consent:\n(1)Matters directly related to national security, national defense security, public safety, public health, and major public interests;\n(2)Necessary for activities such as criminal investigation, prosecution, trial and judgment execution;\n(3)To protect your or other individuals\' life, property and other major legitimate rights and interests but it is difficult to obtain your consent;\n(4)Personal information that you have disclosed yourself;\n(5)Information collected from legal public channels;\n(6)Necessary for entering into and performing contracts;\n(7)Necessary to maintain the safe and stable operation of products or services;\n(8)Other special circumstances stipulated in laws and regulations.\n\nIn addition, for data that has been anonymized and the recipient cannot recover or re-identify the personal information subject, in accordance with legal provisions, its sharing, transfer and public disclosure are not subject to the above restrictions, and such data processing does not require further notification and obtaining your consent. \n\n3. Storage and protection measures of personal information\n\n3.1. Storage of personal information\n\nStorage period: During your use of ECBOT products and/or services, unless you actively delete or refuse collection through system settings, we will continue to retain and use the personal information you provide in the process of providing services.\n\n3.2. Personal information protection\n\n3.2.1 Security measures\n\n(1)We have adopted security protection measures that comply with industry standards to ensure that your personal information will not be subject to unauthorized access, public disclosure, use, modification, damage or loss. We will take all reasonable and feasible measures to protect information security.\n(2)To ensure data confidentiality, we will use encryption technology; at the same time, we will use reliable security protection mechanisms to prevent malicious attacks from threatening the data.\n(3)Implement strict access control policies to ensure that only authorized personnel can access personal information, and sign confidentiality agreements with all employees and partners who come into contact with personal information to clarify their job responsibilities and behavioral norms. Violators will be held responsible. responsibility.\n(4)Regularly organize security and privacy protection training courses to enhance all employees’ awareness of the importance of protecting personal information.\n(5)Only collect necessary information related to the service, and only retain your personal information for the period required to achieve the purposes stated in this policy. If it exceeds this period or has no legal basis, we will delete it in a timely manner.\n\n3.2.2. Safety reminder\n\n(1)The Internet environment is not absolutely secure, so we recommend that you avoid sending sensitive personal information via email, instant messaging, or other unencrypted methods.\n(2)Although we strive to ensure the security of the platform, we cannot fully guarantee the absolute security of any information transmitted via the Internet. If personal information is leaked due to damage to physical, technical or management protection facilities and legitimate rights and interests are damaged, we will bear responsibility according to law.\n(3)When using the Traditional Chinese Medicine Tongue Diagnosis service, please do not upload or share personal information that you consider sensitive, and do not spread it to others through the server. Otherwise, the user will bear the risk of privacy leakage.\n(4)Please do not disclose key information such as property accounts, bank cards, credit cards, third-party payment accounts and their passwords in the Tongue HealthChecker diagnosis service. You will be responsible for any losses caused thereby.\n(5)For acts of counterfeiting or misappropriating the name of others, ECBOT has the right to immediately delete relevant user information and prohibit relevant users from continuing to use the Tongue HealthChecker diagnosis service based on the actual situation.\n\n3.2.3. Security incident notification and response\n\n(1)In response to network security incidents, we have formulated emergency plans that can promptly handle various security risks including system vulnerabilities, viruses, and network attacks, and quickly initiate emergency responses and take remedial measures when security incidents occur.\n(2)Once a personal information security incident occurs, we will promptly notify the affected users of the basic situation of the incident, possible impacts, disposal measures that have been or will be taken, user self-prevention suggestions, and instructions for users in accordance with the requirements of laws and regulations. Remedies. Notifications can be made through various methods such as emails, letters, phone calls, push notifications, etc. When it is difficult to notify each one individually, we will choose a reasonable and effective way to issue announcements.\n(3)If you find that your personal information is at risk of leakage or has been leaked, please immediately contact ECBOT according to the contact information in Chapter 8 [How to Contact Us] of this Privacy Policy so that we can take timely measures.\n\n4. Use of Cookies and Tracking Technologies\n\nWhen you use Traditional Chinese Medicine Tongue Diagnosis and related services, we may use cookies and other similar technologies (such as device identification words) to send information to your device. These technologies are designed to collect and identify relevant information when you access and use this product. We solemnly promise not to use Cookies for any purpose other than those specified in this Privacy Policy. We use this type of technology mainly to:\n\n4.1. Ensure the safe and efficient operation of products and services\n\n   We may set security and authentication-related cookies or anonymous identifiers to verify the security of your login, prevent account theft, fraud and other illegal activities, and optimize service efficiency and response speed.\n\n4.2. Provide convenient user experience\n\n   These technologies help simplify the process of repeatedly filling in personal information, such as implementing one-click login functions, recording search history, etc.\n\n5.Your rights to personal information management\n\nIn compliance with relevant Chinese and international laws, regulations and standards, we guarantee that you have the following rights regarding personal information management:\n\n5.1.Access and correction of personal information\n\n5.1.1.You have the right to view and correct your personal information at any time, including but not limited to tongue photos, comprehensive analysis results, etc. involved in [Comprehensive Tongue Analysis]. When modifying important information such as mobile phone number and WeChat binding, we will verify your identity again to ensure account security.\n\n5.1.2.If you need to access other personal information generated during the use of TCM Tongue Diagnosis, we will provide the required information after reasonable request and after identity verification. If you cannot access or change the information through regular channels, you can contact us through Chapter 8 [How to Contact Us], and we will respond to your access request within 15 working days.\n\n5.2.Deletion of personal information\n\n5.2.1.You can apply to delete personal information by contacting us through the method mentioned in Chapter 8 of this Privacy Policy. After identity verification, we will perform the deletion operation for you.\n\n5.2.2.You can make a request to delete personal information under the following circumstances:\n\n(1)When our personal information processing violates laws and regulations;\n(2)Collecting and using your personal information without your consent;\n(3)We have violated the personal information processing agreement with you;\n(4)You no longer use our products or services, or have canceled your account;\n(5)We terminate service operations.\n\n5.2.3 Regarding your deletion request, after confirmation, we will promptly notify the third-party entity that obtained your personal information from us and request it to delete it as well, unless otherwise provided by law or the entity obtains your independent authorization. We will respond and process the deletion request within 15 working days after receiving it.\n\n5.3.Equipment license management\n\n   In the process of providing services, we may need you to enable some device permissions, such as notifications, albums, cameras, etc. access permissions. You have the right to turn off some or all permissions in the device [Settings] at any time, thereby refusing us to collect the corresponding personal information. The permission display and closing methods may be different on different devices. Please refer to the instructions or policies provided by the device and system developers.\n\n5.4.Account cancellation\n\n   You can apply to cancel your account at any time by informing us through the contact information in Chapter 8 of this policy. After verifying your identity, we will cancel your account or delete relevant information for you. After the account is canceled, we will stop providing services and delete your personal information (including information stored on the server) according to your request, unless otherwise provided by laws and regulations.\n\n5.5.Obtain a copy of personal information\n\n   You have the right to obtain a copy of your personal information by contacting us through the contact information in Chapter 8. After identity verification, we will process your request within 30 days. Where technically feasible, we may also directly transfer a copy of your personal information to a third party designated by you upon your request.\n\n5.6.Withdrawal of consent\n\n   You have the right to withdraw your authorization for personal information processing at any time by contacting us through Chapter 8 of this policy. After identity verification, we will process your request within 15 working days. Please note that each business function requires basic personal information to complete. If you withdraw your consent or authorization, we may be unable to continue to provide you with the corresponding services and stop processing the corresponding personal information. However, your previous authorization revocation decision will not affect our personal information processing activities based on previous authorization.\n\n6.Processing of children’s personal information\n\n6.1.Our products, websites and services are mainly for adult users. Minors are not allowed to create independent accounts without the express consent of their parents or legal guardians.\n\n6.2.According to our definition of children, we regard individuals under the age of 14 as children and follow relevant laws and regulations to protect the security of their personal information.\n\n6.3.If we discover that we have accidentally collected personal information from children without valid consent from parents or legal guardians, we will take immediate steps to delete such information as quickly as possible.\n\n\n7.Privacy Policy Updates and Notices\n\n7.1. ECBOT has the right to revise this privacy policy from time to time. You should carefully read the changed privacy terms and continue to use the products or services provided by ECBOT after confirming your agreement. If you continue to use the services of TCM Tongue Diagnosis after the revision of the Privacy Policy, you will be deemed to have accepted and agreed to the revised Privacy Policy. If you do not agree to the modified content, you should immediately stop using our services.\n\n7.2. We will not reduce your rights under this Privacy Policy without your explicit consent. All policy updates will be posted on this page.\n\n7.3. For major changes, in addition to announcing them on the page, we will also notify users in a more prominent way. For example, for some services, we may use small program notifications, pop-up prompts, etc. to detail the specific changes in the privacy policy. content.\n\n7.4. The following situations are considered major changes to this policy:\n\n(1)Fundamental changes in our service model, including but not limited to the purpose, type, use method, etc. of processing personal information;\n(2)Major adjustments to the company\'s ownership structure and organizational structure, such as changes in ownership resulting from business reorganization, bankruptcy and mergers and acquisitions;\n(3)Changes in the main objects of sharing, transfer or public disclosure of personal information;\n(4)Significant changes in the way you participate in the processing of personal information and exercise related rights;\n(5)The responsible department, contact information and complaint channels for personal information security have changed;\n(6)When the personal information security impact assessment report shows that there is a high risk.\n\n7.5. If you do not accept any updates to the Privacy Policy, please immediately stop using the Traditional Chinese Medicine Tongue Diagnosis Service; if you continue to use it, it will be deemed to have accepted ECBOT\'s modifications to this policy.\n\n8.Contact us\n\nIf you have any questions, comments, suggestions or complaints about this Privacy Policy, you can contact us through the following methods:\n\nEmail: ecbot602@gmail.com \n\n9.Dispute Resolution\n\nRegarding this Privacy Policy and any disputes arising from our processing of your personal information, you can submit feedback to TCM Tongue Diagnosis at any time and request a response.\n";
